  "content": {
    "id": "p12-q10-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "Let $P(x)$ be a polynomial. Prove that $a-b$ is a factor of $P(a)-P(b)$ for all integers $a$ and $b$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$P(a)-P(b)=(a-b)\\displaystyle\\sum_{k=1}^{n}c_k\\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}a^{k-1-j}b^j$.\n\nApply the difference-of-powers identity to each nonconstant term.",
      "worked": "Write $P(x)=c_nx^n+\\cdots+c_1x+c_0$. For each positive integer $k$,\n$$a^k-b^k=(a-b)\\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}a^{k-1-j}b^j.$$\nTherefore,\n$$\\begin{align*}P(a)-P(b)&=\\sum_{k=1}^{n}c_k(a^k-b^k)\\\\P(a)-P(b)&=\\sum_{k=1}^{n}c_k(a-b)\\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}a^{k-1-j}b^j\\\\P(a)-P(b)&=(a-b)\\sum_{k=1}^{n}c_k\\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}a^{k-1-j}b^j.\\end{align*}$$\nHence $a-b$ is an algebraic factor of $P(a)-P(b)$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 55
  },
